*> Credentials in VALUE clauses and MOVEs, sensitive items shown with
*> DISPLAY, and commands run from data items. Names that only
*> describe the data (PASSWORD-LENGTH, PIN-RETRY-COUNT) and names
*> that merely contain a marker (SPINDLE, PINNED) are not reported.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. SECURITY.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  DB-PASSWORD         PIC X(16) VALUE "tiger".
01  API-SECRET          PIC X(32) VALUE SPACES.
01  PASSWORD-LENGTH     PIC 9(4) VALUE 16.
01  CUSTOMER-PIN        PIC 9(4).
01  PIN-RETRY-COUNT     PIC 9 VALUE 0.
01  SPINDLE-ID          PIC X(8) VALUE "S1".
01  PINNED-FLAG         PIC X VALUE "N".
01  CARD-CVV            PIC 999.
01  SHELL-LINE          PIC X(80).
01  USER-NAME           PIC X(20).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    MOVE "s3cr3t" TO API-SECRET
    MOVE SPACES TO DB-PASSWORD
    MOVE 1234 TO CUSTOMER-PIN
    DISPLAY "LOGIN " USER-NAME " " DB-PASSWORD
    DISPLAY CUSTOMER-PIN
    DISPLAY CARD-CVV
    DISPLAY PASSWORD-LENGTH PIN-RETRY-COUNT SPINDLE-ID PINNED-FLAG
    CALL "SYSTEM" USING "ls -l"
    STRING "grep " USER-NAME " /etc/passwd" DELIMITED BY SIZE
        INTO SHELL-LINE
    CALL "SYSTEM" USING BY CONTENT SHELL-LINE
    STOP RUN.
